{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/duckdb/duckdb/issues/25164","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/duckdb/duckdb","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/duckdb/duckdb/issues/25164/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/duckdb/duckdb/issues/25164/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/duckdb/duckdb/issues/25164/events","html_url":"https://github.com/duckdb/duckdb/issues/25164","id":5295474491,"node_id":"I_kwDOCEU65s8AAAABO6KHOw","number":25164,"title":"Parallel CSV reader emits duplicate rows on files with \\r\\r\\n line endings","user":{"login":"mdragovan-blip","id":322964866,"node_id":"U_kgDOE0ANgg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/322964866?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdragovan-blip","html_url":"https://github.com/mdragovan-blip","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdragovan-blip/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdragovan-blip/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdragovan-blip/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdragovan-blip/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdragovan-blip/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdragovan-blip/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdragovan-blip/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdragovan-blip/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdragovan-blip/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":5778180827,"node_id":"LA_kwDOCEU65s8AAAABWGgK2w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/duckdb/duckdb/labels/reproduced","name":"reproduced","color":"0E8A16","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-08-31T01:25:35Z","updated_at":"2026-09-07T10:48:58Z","closed_at":"2026-09-07T10:48:58Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### What happens?\n\nWhen a CSV file uses `\\r\\r\\n` as its line terminator, the parallel CSV reader emits byte-identical duplicates of rows that appear exactly once in the source file. The duplicated rows are well-formed and valid — they are simply returned twice. Reading the same file with `parallel=false` returns the correct row count with no duplicates.\n\nThe number of duplicates scales with the number of buffer boundaries in the file: a smaller `buffer_size` (or a larger file) produces more duplicates. The result is deterministic for a given file and buffer size — it does not vary between runs or with the thread count — which suggests a boundary-handling error rather than a race.\n\nFiles with ordinary `\\r\\n` or `\\n` terminators are unaffected.\n\nThis is silent data corruption: no error, no warning, and nothing in `reject_errors`. It was found only because row counts were being cross-checked against an independent count of the source file.\n\n### To Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport duckdb\n\nwith open(\"rr.csv\", \"w\", newline=\"\") as f:\n    f.write(\"id,val\\r\\r\\n\")\n    for i in range(10000):\n        f.write(f\"{i},x\\r\\r\\n\")\n\ncon = duckdb.connect()\ncon.execute(\"SET threads=8\")\n\nq = \"\"\"SELECT COUNT(*) AS rows, COUNT(DISTINCT id) AS distinct_ids\n       FROM read_csv('rr.csv', auto_detect=false, header=true, delim=',',\n            columns={'id':'BIGINT','val':'VARCHAR'},\n            strict_mode=false, ignore_errors=true,\n            max_line_size=2048, buffer_size=4096, parallel=%s)\"\"\"\n\nprint(\"parallel=true :\", con.execute(q % \"true\").fetchone())\nprint(\"parallel=false:\", con.execute(q % \"false\").fetchone())\n```\n\nOutput:\n\n```\nparallel=true : (10002, 10000)\nparallel=false: (10000, 10000)\n```\n\nThe file contains 10,000 data rows. The parallel reader returns 10,002 rows containing only 10,000 distinct ids. The duplicated ids in this case are 1943 and 6039.\n\n### Scaling with buffer size\n\nSame generator, `threads=8`, varying row count and `buffer_size`:\n\n| rows    | buffer_size | rows returned | extra |\n|---------|-------------|---------------|-------|\n| 10,000  | 4,096       | 10,002        | +2    |\n| 10,000  | 16,384      | 10,001        | +1    |\n| 10,000  | 65,536      | 10,000        |  0    |\n| 200,000 | 4,096       | 200,027       | +27   |\n| 200,000 | 16,384      | 200,008       | +8    |\n| 200,000 | 65,536      | 200,002       | +2    |\n\nIdentical results at `threads=4` and `threads=8`.\n\n### Only `\\r\\r\\n` is affected\n\nSame 200,000-row generator, 31 columns, `buffer_size=131072`, `threads=8`:\n\n| line ending | expected | returned | diff |\n|-------------|----------|----------|------|\n| `\\r\\r\\n`    | 200,000  | 200,001  | +1   |\n| `\\r\\n`      | 200,000  | 200,000  |  0   |\n| `\\n`        | 200,000  | 200,000  |  0   |\n\n### Real-world case\n\nFound on ~20 GB option-quote CSVs (~83M rows, 31 columns) written with `\\r\\r\\n` endings, read at the **default** buffer size:\n\n```\nrecords in source (grep -c):  82,984,768\nparallel=true              :  82,984,769 rows, 1 duplicate group, 41 rejects   (35s)\nparallel=false             :  82,984,768 rows, 0 duplicate groups, 40 rejects  (267s)\n```\n\nNote that the reject count also differs by one between the two paths.\n\nAcross a batch of 15 such files, 9 were affected, with 1–2 duplicated rows each. Because the duplicates are valid, well-formed rows, they are invisible to any schema- or error-based validation.\n\nA second, possibly related symptom on the same files: with `\\r\\r\\n` endings the reader consumes `\\r\\r` as the terminator and leaves the `\\n` attached to the front of the first field, so `symbol` arrives as `\"\\nSPXW\"` rather than `\"SPXW\"` on nearly every row. That happens under both parallel and sequential reads, so it may be a separate issue.\n\n### OS:\n\nmacOS 26.5.1, x86_64\n\n### DuckDB Version:\n\n1.5.2 (CLI), also reproduced on 1.4.4 and 1.5.5\n\n### DuckDB Client:\n\nCLI and Python\n\n### Hardware:\n\n2019 Mac Pro, 16-core Intel Xeon, 256 GB RAM\n\n### Full Name:\n\nMark Dragovan\n\n### Affiliation:\n\nDRD\n\n### Did you include all relevant configuration (e.g., CPU architecture, Linux distribution) to reproduce the issue?\n\n- [x] Yes, I have\n\n### Did you include all code required to reproduce the issue?\n\n- [x] Yes, I have\n\n### Did you include all relevant data sets for reproducing the issue?\n\nNot applicable - the reproduction does not require a data set","closed_by":{"login":"Mytherin","id":3978469,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5Nzg0Njk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3978469?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mytherin","html_url":"https://github.com/Mytherin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mytherin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mytherin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mytherin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mytherin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mytherin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mytherin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mytherin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mytherin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mytherin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/duckdb/duckdb/issues/25164/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/duckdb/duckdb/issues/25164/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}